        {"q": "According to CFA Institute’s position paper A Comprehensive Business Reporting Model, investors:", "opts": ["prefer decision relevance over reliability", "prefer the indirect method for the cash flow statement", "prefer historical cost over fair value for assets and liabilities"], "ans": 0, "hint": "The paper argues for information that shows economic reality.", "why": "The paper says investors prefer <b>decision relevance over reliability</b>, and stresses <b>fair value</b>, neutrality and the <b>direct</b> cash flow format. B and C are the opposite of what it recommends."}
